[0.019, "o", "\u001b[2mid:   \u001b[0m \u001b[2mwindows-build-failure\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2mnotes:\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAdding x86_64-pc-windows-msvc to the release matrix surfaced a latent type error\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2min the `cfg(not(unix))` arm of `is_executable_file` (src/cli/mod.rs): it passed\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2m`std::fs::Metadata::is_file` as a function path to `Result::is_ok_and`, but\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2m`is_ok_and` hands the `Metadata` over BY VALUE while `is_file` borrows it, so the\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2mpath form never coerced. The `cfg(unix)` arm already used a closure and was fine.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n       \u001b[2mThe branch had never been compiled by anything - CI is Linux-only and the crate\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2mhad no Windows target - so the first thing ever to type-check it was the release\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2mbuild.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n       \u001b[2mFixed with a closure, verified by cross-checking the crate for\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2mx86_64-pc-windows-msvc, and guarded by a new Windows build job in ci.yml so this\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2mclass of bug fails on a push instead of at release time. Build-only for now: the\u001b[0m\r\r\n       \u001b[2me2e suite makes POSIX assumptions and porting it is separate work.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.007, "o", "\u001b[33m(master) \u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m$ \u001b[0m"]
